WEBVTT

1
00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:47.000
In the earlier verses of Chapter 14,

2
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.041
Lord Krishna described the three gunas

3
00:00:50.041 --> 00:00:53.541
sattva, rajas and tamas in detail –

4
00:00:53.541 --> 00:00:58.000
sattva meaning knowledge and peace,

5
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.208
rajas meaning desire and the tendency
toward action,

6
00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:07.291
and tamas meaning ignorance, laziness,
and inertia.

7
00:01:07.291 --> 00:01:10.208
Now in verses 14.14 and 14.15,

8
00:01:10.208 --> 00:01:12.416
He explains that whichever guna is dominant

9
00:01:12.416 --> 00:01:14.166
at the time of death

10
00:01:14.166 --> 00:01:17.166
determines the soul’s next journey

11
00:01:17.166 --> 00:01:19.041
and destination.

12
00:01:24.125 --> 00:01:26.458
If a person dies

13
00:01:26.458 --> 00:01:29.000
with sattva Guna predominant,

14
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.000
they attain the pure and elevated realms where

15
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.458
souls endowed with knowledge dwell.

16
00:01:36.458 --> 00:01:39.291
Higher realms like Brahmaloka and Janaloka

17
00:01:39.291 --> 00:01:43.541
are beyond the influence of rajas and tamas.

18
00:01:43.541 --> 00:01:47.041
There the soul finds an environment conducive

19
00:01:47.041 --> 00:01:48.833
to spiritual progress.

20
00:01:48.833 --> 00:01:52.000
But this is not final liberation, because

21
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.000
even these realms are temporary.

22
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.750
If a person dies under the influence

23
00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.583
of Rajo Guna,

24
00:01:59.583 --> 00:02:01.541
they are reborn among human beings

25
00:02:01.541 --> 00:02:05.541
attached to action and material striving.

26
00:02:05.541 --> 00:02:09.333
They return to a society where desires,

27
00:02:09.333 --> 00:02:11.083
ambitions,

28
00:02:11.083 --> 00:02:14.333
and the craving for material goals are strong.

29
00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:15.625
The result is

30
00:02:15.625 --> 00:02:19.000
a renewed cycle of constant effort and striving,

31
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.291
but with little clarity

32
00:02:20.291 --> 00:02:23.958
about life’s higher purpose.

33
00:02:23.958 --> 00:02:25.541
On the other hand,

34
00:02:25.541 --> 00:02:27.500
a person who dies with Tamo Guna

35
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.416
predominant

36
00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:32.541
is born in lower species –

37
00:02:32.541 --> 00:02:36.000
animals or other inferior life forms.

38
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.708
Such a birth is the result of ignorance,

39
00:02:37.708 --> 00:02:39.583
carelessness,

40
00:02:39.583 --> 00:02:42.500
and lack of spiritual awareness.

41
00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:43.333
Such beings

42
00:02:43.333 --> 00:02:45.625
are deprived of higher intelligence

43
00:02:45.625 --> 00:02:47.041
and must again

44
00:02:47.041 --> 00:02:48.458
make the long journey

45
00:02:48.458 --> 00:02:50.583
of gradual evolution.

46
00:02:50.583 --> 00:02:53.166
Lord Krishna emphasises this truth –

47
00:02:53.166 --> 00:02:54.000
if a person

48
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.750
cultivates sattva Guna

49
00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:59.166
and ultimately rises beyond all three gunas,

50
00:02:59.166 --> 00:03:00.208
they can be free

51
00:03:00.208 --> 00:03:03.958
from this cycle of birth and death.

52
00:03:08.541 --> 00:03:12.583
You may think that the small decisions

53
00:03:12.583 --> 00:03:14.833
and choices of your daily

54
00:03:14.833 --> 00:03:17.250
life are ordinary.

55
00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:20.833
But the truth is – every small decision

56
00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:25.000
builds the atmosphere within you.

57
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.166
The guna in which you live – sattva, rajas,

58
00:03:28.166 --> 00:03:32.416
or tamas – becomes your
permanent companion.

59
00:03:32.416 --> 00:03:33.833
And this companion

60
00:03:33.833 --> 00:03:35.708
does not leave your side

61
00:03:35.708 --> 00:03:38.333
even at the moment of death.

62
00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:43.000
If your life has been spent mostly in sattva –

63
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.375
seeking clarity, doing good deeds,

64
00:03:46.375 --> 00:03:48.000
remaining alert –

65
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.333
then even the final moment will be
filled with peace.

66
00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:53.583
You will depart

67
00:03:53.583 --> 00:03:57.333
from this world in that same calm state,

68
00:03:57.333 --> 00:03:59.375
and your next journey

69
00:03:59.375 --> 00:04:01.666
will reflect that.

70
00:04:01.666 --> 00:04:05.583
But if your daily life has been spent

71
00:04:05.583 --> 00:04:09.041
only in restless running, fulfilling desires,

72
00:04:09.041 --> 00:04:12.416
or in the darkness of ignorance –

73
00:04:12.416 --> 00:04:14.041
that same state

74
00:04:14.041 --> 00:04:17.833
may become your reality going forward.

75
00:04:17.833 --> 00:04:21.166
Just as a student does not prepare

76
00:04:21.166 --> 00:04:24.208
for an exam in one day,

77
00:04:24.208 --> 00:04:28.041
the outcome at the moment of death

78
00:04:28.041 --> 00:04:31.958
is also not determined by a single great deed.

79
00:04:31.958 --> 00:04:36.958
It is determined by your small daily choices –

80
00:04:36.958 --> 00:04:40.875
what you watch, how you speak,

81
00:04:40.875 --> 00:04:43.333
what you give priority to.

82
00:04:43.333 --> 00:04:47.125
So ask yourself –

83
00:04:47.125 --> 00:04:49.916
‘What am I doing today?’

84
00:04:49.916 --> 00:04:51.208
And alongside this,

85
00:04:51.208 --> 00:04:54.208
it is equally important to ask –

86
00:04:54.208 --> 00:04:57.875
‘In which guna am I living?’

87
00:04:57.875 --> 00:05:01.000
Because the way you live…

88
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:01.875
is the way

89
00:05:01.875 --> 00:05:03.625
you depart.

90
00:05:03.625 --> 00:05:08.500
And the way you depart… determines

91
00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.166
where you go next.

92
00:05:11.166 --> 00:05:15.625
So choose your guna with awareness –

93
00:05:15.625 --> 00:05:21.000
it is shaping your soul’s journey.

94
00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:29.708
When you think about ‘legacy,’

95
00:05:29.708 --> 00:05:32.041
what comes to mind?

96
00:05:32.041 --> 00:05:35.166
Property, savings, or objects

97
00:05:35.166 --> 00:05:38.583
to be preserved?

98
00:05:38.583 --> 00:05:42.875
But I want you to think more deeply.

99
00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:45.708
In your family, the true legacy

100
00:05:45.708 --> 00:05:49.125
is not of things – because

101
00:05:49.125 --> 00:05:51.916
things fade away.

102
00:05:51.916 --> 00:05:55.208
The real legacy is of the energy,

103
00:05:55.208 --> 00:05:58.708
the atmosphere, the guna

104
00:05:58.708 --> 00:06:02.625
in which you lived your life.

105
00:06:02.625 --> 00:06:06.958
If your children saw you living in peace,

106
00:06:06.958 --> 00:06:11.125
compassion, and clarity – that sattva

107
00:06:11.125 --> 00:06:15.333
will become part of their emotional memory.

108
00:06:15.333 --> 00:06:18.458
If you spent life in constant ambition

109
00:06:18.458 --> 00:06:21.625
and the race for achievement –

110
00:06:21.625 --> 00:06:26.083
that rajas will leave its imprint within them.

111
00:06:26.083 --> 00:06:29.750
And if your days were filled with irritability,

112
00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:34.000
neglect, or confusion – then however

113
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.916
much else you may have given the family,

114
00:06:37.916 --> 00:06:43.250
the core feeling they inherit is of tamas.

115
00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:47.875
I do not expect perfection from you.

116
00:06:47.875 --> 00:06:52.250
I only expect awareness.

117
00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:56.125
Every time you choose patience

118
00:06:56.125 --> 00:06:57.875
over anger,

119
00:06:57.875 --> 00:07:02.375
understanding over ego, or simplicity
over show –

120
00:07:02.375 --> 00:07:05.250
you are teaching your family

121
00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:09.291
what truly matters.

122
00:07:09.291 --> 00:07:10.500
Legacy is not

123
00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:13.583
in the words written in a will.

124
00:07:13.583 --> 00:07:15.666
It is in what your family

125
00:07:15.666 --> 00:07:20.958
experiences in your absence.

126
00:07:20.958 --> 00:07:24.791
So live each day in a way

127
00:07:24.791 --> 00:07:29.291
that the atmosphere left behind
after your departure

128
00:07:29.291 --> 00:07:33.125
becomes a blessing, not a burden.

129
00:07:33.125 --> 00:07:35.791
Let your dominant guna be one

130
00:07:35.791 --> 00:07:39.041
that lights the path for those you leave behind –

131
00:07:39.041 --> 00:07:42.500
long after you have gone.

132
00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.041
You may think

133
00:07:49.041 --> 00:07:50.916
that your project ends

134
00:07:50.916 --> 00:07:53.083
with the deadline,

135
00:07:53.083 --> 00:07:54.250
or your role

136
00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:55.458
concludes with a promotion

137
00:07:55.458 --> 00:07:59.166
or transfer.

138
00:07:59.166 --> 00:08:01.500
But have you noticed?

139
00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:05.666
The way you carry out one piece of work

140
00:08:05.666 --> 00:08:07.000
often shapes

141
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.250
the nature of the next.

142
00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:11.958
This is not coincidence –

143
00:08:11.958 --> 00:08:14.583
it is your guna moving forward.

144
00:08:14.583 --> 00:08:17.750
When you work in sattva –

145
00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:21.875
with clarity, steadiness, and a spirit of service –

146
00:08:21.875 --> 00:08:25.000
you do not only complete work.

147
00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.916
You also earn trust.

148
00:08:27.916 --> 00:08:31.916
People want to work with you again.

149
00:08:31.916 --> 00:08:35.083
Opportunities come to you on their own.

150
00:08:35.083 --> 00:08:37.250
Even if the job changes,

151
00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:39.333
your inner atmosphere

152
00:08:39.333 --> 00:08:42.166
creates conditions for growth.

153
00:08:42.166 --> 00:08:43.208
But when rajas

154
00:08:43.208 --> 00:08:46.208
dominates – unstable ambition,

155
00:08:46.208 --> 00:08:49.333
stress, and the race for credit –

156
00:08:49.333 --> 00:08:53.208
you complete the work, but bring

157
00:08:53.208 --> 00:08:58.083
more pressure, more disorder,

158
00:08:58.083 --> 00:09:02.125
and the same cycle back into your life.

159
00:09:02.125 --> 00:09:04.625
And tamas?

160
00:09:04.625 --> 00:09:07.291
That guna quietly pulls you toward unfinished

161
00:09:07.291 --> 00:09:11.083
work, indifference, and eventually

162
00:09:11.083 --> 00:09:14.041
stagnation –

163
00:09:14.041 --> 00:09:18.666
until you do not even realise

164
00:09:18.666 --> 00:09:21.291
how far you have drifted.

165
00:09:21.291 --> 00:09:24.833
I am telling you this – your guna

166
00:09:24.833 --> 00:09:26.458
does not only determine

167
00:09:26.458 --> 00:09:29.541
how you work today.

168
00:09:29.541 --> 00:09:33.000
It also determines what kind of work,

169
00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:34.583
what kind of people,

170
00:09:34.583 --> 00:09:39.208
and what kind of environment comes
to you tomorrow.

171
00:09:39.208 --> 00:09:41.625
You carry your guna

172
00:09:41.625 --> 00:09:44.375
into the next role –

173
00:09:44.375 --> 00:09:47.041
whether that is next quarter,

174
00:09:47.041 --> 00:09:49.291
or the next life’s journey.

175
00:09:49.291 --> 00:09:52.875
So choose carefully.

176
00:09:52.875 --> 00:09:56.833
Remember – your thoughts are the navigator

177
00:09:56.833 --> 00:10:00.291
that steers the boat of life to the other shore.
